 ],
 "text": "What if every government on earth left tomorrow and never came back? No presidents, no parliaments, no tax office. Day 1. No new laws, no new taxes. Every group chat goes wild and somebody's uncle declares himself mayor. Day 2. The traffic lights still work, nobody's in charge of them. Somebody's code is just running in a basement. Day 3. The first people to organize anything are the neighborhood group chats. One of them already has a treasurer and a strict no voice notes rule. Week 2. Trash piles up on every corner. Every city finds out who actually kept things running and it wasn't the people on TV. Month 1. Businesses with clear systems keep paying people on time. The ones running on one person's memory just stop. Year 1. The new governments are basically group chats with rules and an approval step. Systems beat titles. Want the five starter skills I use to run my company? Comment AI and I'll send them to you free."
